  "content": "# Implementing a Bounded LRU Cache in Python\n\n## Overview\n\nA **Least Recently Used (LRU) cache** is a data structure that evicts the least recently used item when the cache reaches its capacity. This is a common pattern in systems where memory is limited but access patterns are skewed \u2014 frequently accessed items should stay in memory, while stale items are discarded.\n\nPython's `collections.OrderedDict` provides an ideal foundation for an LRU cache because it maintains insertion order and supports moving items to the end in O(1) time.\n\n---\n\n## The Core Idea\n\n1. **Store items** in an `OrderedDict` where keys are cache keys and values are cached values.\n2. **On `get(key)`**: If the key exists, move it to the end (marking it as most recently used) and return the value. If not, return a default.\n3. **On `put(key, value)`**: If the key already exists, update its value and move it to the end. If the key is new and the cache is at capacity, evict the first item (least recently used). Then insert the new item at the end.\n\nThe key insight: **the first item in the `OrderedDict` is the least recently used; the last item is the most recently used.**\n\n---\n\n## Complete Implementation\n\n```python\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    \"\"\"\n    A bounded LRU cache using collections.OrderedDict.\n    \n    - get(key): Returns the value for key if present, else default.\n                Marks the key as most recently used.\n    - put(key, value): Inserts or updates a key-value pair.\n                If the cache is at capacity and the key is new,\n                evicts the least recently used item.\n    \n    All operations are O(1) average time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize the LRU cache with a given capacity.\n        \n        Args:\n            capacity: Maximum number of items the cache can hold.\n                       Must be a positive integer.\n        \n        Raises:\n            ValueError: If capacity is less than 1.\n        \"\"\"\n        if capacity < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"Capacity must be at least 1\")\n        \n        self.capacity = capacity\n        self.cache: OrderedDict[Any, Any",
